<title>USA: Dow slide unofficially ranks as 2nd largest ever.</title>
<headline>Dow slide unofficially ranks as 2nd largest ever.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials tumbled 192 points on Monday, a sell-off that unofficially ranks as the second largest in point terms in the average's history.</p>
<p>The Dow's last comparable decline in point terms occurred on October 13, 1989, when it slid 190.58 points or 6.91 percent. Today's loss, which amounted to about 2.47 percent, ranked nowhere near the all-time top 10 in percentage terms.</p>
<p>The Dow's largest loss remains the 508-point &quot;Black Monday&quot; plunge of October 19, 1987.</p>
<p>The following list includes the Dow Jones Industrial Average's 10 largest losses in point and percentage terms.  </p>
